The error points to line 4, the `SELECT ... INTO` statement. `ORA-01403: no data found` means that statement returned no rows. Given your note, the likely cause is a department id whose manager lookup produces no row, for example because the department has no manager or there is no matching employee row. The repair is to handle `NO_DATA_FOUND` and return `NULL`.

The replacement below has not been compiled. It changes only the exception handling; the query and declarations are kept as supplied.

